    "bottomLine": "The ViscoSoft Select High Density is the best mattress topper for most beds because it pairs a published 3.1 lb/ft³ foam density with a medium-firm feel, corner straps and a washable cover.",
    "description": "The Select High Density is the topper we would put on most beds first. It is a slab of gel-infused memory foam, and ViscoSoft lists the foam at 3.1 lb/ft³, a figure most budget brands never publish. Density is the best clue to how long foam holds its shape, so that number matters. ViscoSoft describes the feel as medium-firm, which means it softens a hard mattress without letting your hips sink far, a good middle ground for combination sleepers and people with sore backs. Vertical airflow channels are cut into the foam, which the maker says help release heat. The removable cover is machine-washable, and its underside is a beaded mesh meant to grip the mattress, backed up by elastic corner straps. That combination addresses the most common topper complaint, sliding. ViscoSoft sells it in 2, 3 and 4 inch heights; the 4-inch version is described as firmer. The maker's store offers a 90-day money-back period. Its site lists a 5-year warranty on toppers, while some reviews cite 3 years, so confirm the terms on the listing. Check today's price, since ViscoSoft discounts often."
