      "By far the most expensive topper in this guide",
      "Too soft for most back and stomach sleepers with back pain",
      "Tempur does not accept topper returns directly"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The deepest pressure relief here for side sleepers on a firm mattress, at a premium price.",
    "description": "The TEMPUR-Adapt + Cooling is 3 inches of the same TEMPUR material Tempur-Pedic uses in its mattresses, under a cool-to-the-touch cover that Tempur says keeps that feel after washing. Tempur describes the foam as extra-soft. That makes it our pick for side sleepers whose mattress pushes back too hard at the shoulder and hip, and owners commonly report that it takes the pressure out of a firm bed. It is not the right topper for everyone. Back and stomach sleepers with back pain may sink too far into it, and memory foam this soft still sleeps warmer than latex, cooling cover or not. Retail listings describe corner straps to hold it in place. The warranty is a 10-year limited term, and reviewers note that Tempur treats toppers as personal items it will not take back, though orders through Amazon fall under Amazon's own return policy. Price is the big hurdle: Tempur lists the queen at $519 at the time of writing. Amazon has frequently discounted it during sales, and TechRadar has reported that Amazon sells only the Cooling version. Check today's price before buying."
