    "description": "Pure Green, sold by Sleep On Latex, is a slab of natural latex made with what the maker calls an enhanced version of the Dunlop process. It comes in 1, 2 and 3 inch heights and in soft, medium and firm, and the maker publishes the numbers for each: soft at 4.0 lb/ft³ with a 25 percent IFD of 20 lbf, medium at 4.7 lb/ft³ and 34 lbf, and firm at 5.9 lb/ft³ and 46 lbf. Those figures make it unusually easy to choose. For back pain, or to firm up a mattress that has gone slightly soft, the maker recommends the firm grade at 2 inches minimum and preferably 3. For a side sleeper softening a hard bed, the soft grade is the pick. Latex pushes back rather than sinking slowly, so it is easier to move on and sleeps cooler than memory foam. The trade-offs are weight and price. A 3-inch firm queen is a heavy slab, and it has no straps, so plan on the optional cotton cover or a deep-pocket sheet. The maker offers 30-day returns with a free return label and a 5-year warranty. Some buyers find the medium softer than expected, so pick firm if in doubt. Check today's price."
