      "Ships compressed in a small box"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Only 1 inch of memory foam, so less contouring than the Tempur or Lucid",
      "No cover and no straps",
      "Zinus asks you to unbox it within 72 hours"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A budget topper with a supportive base layer, better for back sleepers than a soft slab.",
    "description": "The Zinus Green Tea topper is built differently from the other budget picks. Instead of one slab of memory foam, it has 1 inch of memory foam on top, infused with green tea, charcoal and plant oil, over 2 inches of high-density base foam. In principle, that firmer base limits how far you sink, which makes it a better fit for back sleepers than a soft 3-inch slab and a weaker one for side sleepers who want deep contouring. Zinus says the infusions help keep the foam fresh; we would not buy it for that. We would buy it because it adds a real comfort layer to a hard mattress at a low price, from a brand with a long record on Amazon. The foam is CertiPUR-US certified, and the warranty is a 5-year limited term, longer than most budget toppers carry. It ships compressed, and Zinus asks that you unpack it within 72 hours so it expands properly; expect some new-foam smell for the first day or two. There is no cover and no strap system, so add a zippered cover or a deep-pocket sheet. Zinus sells several green tea toppers, so confirm the 3-inch, two-layer version. Check today's price."
